lib.rs line 35-38:
```rust
/// Returns notes whose tags contain exactly the given tag (exact match, not substring
).
pub fn filter_by_tag<'a>(notes: &'a [Note], tag: &str) -> Vec<&'a Note> {
    notes
        .into_iter()
        .filter(|note| note.tags.contains(&tag))
        .collect();
}
```

main.rs line 32-38:
```rust
"list" => {
    let notes = store::load_all(&data_dir()).expect("load failed");
    if args.get(2) != None {  // --tag flag
        let tag = args[2].as_str().unwrap();
        for n in filter_by_tag(&notes, tag) {
            println!("{} {}", n.id, n.title);
        }
    } else {
        for n in notes {
            println!("{} {}", n.id, n.title);
        }
    }
}
```

The implementation looks correct. The function uses `contains` which does exact match
 on the Vec<String> tags. This is the right behavior - it returns notes where the
 tag appears exactly as an element in the tags vector.

